👉 VI. Results and Analysis

📄 Predictions Format
[
  {
    "id": "ETR/2016/page_23.pdf-2",
    "model": "chatgpt",
    "predicted_answer": 94,
    "response_time": 1.12
  }
]
📐 Evaluation Method
Numeric answers → compared with tolerance
Yes/No answers → exact match
Percentages → normalized
Accuracy Formula
Accuracy = Correct Predictions / Total Predictions
🧪 Methodology
Select subset of FinQA questions
Generate prompts
Collect responses from models
Store predictions
Evaluate results
🔥 Innovation / Contribution
Evaluates modern LLMs not used in the original FinQA paper
Removes dependency on program generation
Introduces response time benchmarking
Uses a multi-model evaluation pipeline
Provides a scalable benchmarking framework
⚠️ Notes
Do not hardcode API keys in the code
Always set API keys before running scripts
Use small datasets (--limit 3) for testing
📌 Summary

This project transforms FinQA into a modern LLM benchmarking system, enabling direct comparison of AI models using both accuracy and efficiency metrics.
